IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc17-privilege.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, section 488.1: examination, copying or seizure of documents in a lawyer's possession where solicitor-client
-- privilege is claimed. Layer 1: the law, objectively. Same conventions as ccc17-dna-orders.l4. Seam input: `s 321 the thing is a document` (ccc12, MAYBE BOOLEAN).
-- A duty gated by "Where" or "On an application" answers JUST FALSE when the gate fails; a "may" gated by "where" is in fork group G1 (JUST FALSE, for a lawyer).

§ `Section 488.1 -- Definitions`

-- covers: 488.1(1) "custodian", 488.1(1)
-- jural: none
-- src:9916 | custodian means a person in whose custody a package is placed pursuant to subsection (2); (gardien)
@ref s 488.1(1) "custodian" (src:9916)
GIVEN `the person is a person in whose custody a package is placed pursuant to subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 488.1(1) custodian` MEANS
    IF `the person is a person in whose custody a package is placed pursuant to subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "custodian means a person in whose custody a package is placed pursuant to subsection (2)"

-- covers: 488.1(1) "document"
-- jural: none
-- src:9917 | document, for the purposes of this section, has the same meaning as in section 321; (document)
@ref s 488.1(1) "document" (src:9917)
GIVEN `s 321 the thing is a document` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 488.1(1) document` MEANS `s 321 the thing is a document`   -- "document, for the purposes of this section, has the same meaning as in section 321": the answer of section 321, carried through

-- covers: 488.1(1) "judge"
-- jural: none
-- src:9918 | judge means a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the province where the seizure was made; (juge)
@ref s 488.1(1) "judge" (src:9918)
GIVEN `the person is a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is that of the province where the seizure was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 488.1(1) judge` MEANS
    IF `the person is a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction` AND `the court is that of the province where the seizure was made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "judge means a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the province where the seizure was made"

DECLARE `s 488.1(1) description of the lawyer` IS ONE OF
    `s 488.1(1) an advocate, lawyer or notary`
    `s 488.1(1) a barrister or solicitor`
    `s 488.1(1) neither`

-- covers: 488.1(1) "lawyer"
-- fork: F8
-- jural: none
-- src:9919 | lawyer means, in the Province of Quebec, an advocate, lawyer or notary and, in any other province, a barrister or solicitor; (avocat)
@ref s 488.1(1) "lawyer" (src:9919)
-- "means, in the Province of Quebec, an advocate, lawyer or notary and, in any other province, a barrister or solicitor": a territory is not a province, so the definition says nothing for Yukon, the
-- Northwest Territories and Nunavut (fork F8).
GIVEN province IS A `Province or territory`
      description IS A `s 488.1(1) description of the lawyer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 488.1(1) lawyer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF province EQUALS Yukon OR province EQUALS `Northwest Territories` OR province EQUALS Nunavut THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF province EQUALS Quebec AND description EQUALS `s 488.1(1) an advocate, lawyer or notary` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF province EQUALS Quebec THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "lawyer means, in the Province of Quebec, an advocate, lawyer or notary"
        IF description EQUALS `s 488.1(1) a barrister or solicitor` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in any other province, a barrister or solicitor"

-- covers: 488.1(1) "officer"
-- jural: none
-- src:9920 | officer means a peace officer or public officer. (fonctionnaire)
@ref s 488.1(1) "officer" (src:9920)
GIVEN `s 2 peace officer: the person is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2 public officer: the person is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 488.1(1) officer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 2 peace officer: the person is one` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 2 public officer: the person is one` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 2 peace officer: the person is one` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND `s 2 public officer: the person is one` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "officer means a peace officer or public officer"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text)

§ `Section 488.1 -- Claim of solicitor-client privilege, application to a judge, custody`

-- covers: 488.1(2), 488.1(2)(a)
-- jural: a lawyer and the client claiming privilege > an officer > right
-- src:9922 | (2) Where an officer acting under the authority of this or any other Act of Parliament is about to examine, copy or seize a document in the possession of a lawyer who claims that a named client of his has a solicitor-client privilege in respect of that document, the officer shall, without examining or making copies of the document,
-- src:9923 | (a) seize the document and place it in a package and suitably seal and identify the package; and
-- src:9924 | (b) place the package in the custody of the sheriff of the district or county in which the seizure was made or, if there is agreement in writing that a specified person act as custodian, in the custody of that person.
@ref s 488.1(2) (src:9922-9924)
GIVEN `an officer acting under the authority of this or any other Act of Parliament is about to examine, copy or seize a document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is in the possession of a lawyer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the lawyer claims that a named client of theirs has a solicitor-client privilege in respect of the document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 488.1(2) the officer shall, without examining or making copies of the document, seize it and place it in a package, suitably sealed and identified` MEANS
    IF `an officer acting under the authority of this or any other Act of Parliament is about to examine, copy or seize a document` AND `the document is in the possession of a lawyer` AND `the lawyer claims that a named client of theirs has a solicitor-client privilege in respect of the document`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an officer acting under the authority of this or any other Act of Parliament is about to examine, copy or seize a document in the possession of a lawyer who claims that a named client of his has a solicitor-client privilege in respect of that document"

DECLARE `s 488.1(2)(b) custodian` IS ONE OF
    `s 488.1(2)(b) the sheriff of the district or county in which the seizure was made`
    `s 488.1(2)(b) the specified person named in a written agreement`

@ref s 488.1(2)(b) (the custodian) (src:9922-9924)
GIVEN `an officer acting under the authority of this or any other Act of Parliament is about to examine, copy or seize a document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is in the possession of a lawyer who claims that a named client of theirs has a solicitor-client privilege in respect of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is agreement in writing that a specified person act as custodian` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 488.1(2)(b) custodian`
`s 488.1(2)(b) the package shall be placed in the custody of` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`an officer acting under the authority of this or any other Act of Parliament is about to examine, copy or seize a document` AND `the document is in the possession of a lawyer who claims that a named client of theirs has a solicitor-client privilege in respect of it`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF `there is agreement in writing that a specified person act as custodian` THEN JUST `s 488.1(2)(b) the specified person named in a written agreement`
        OTHERWISE JUST `s 488.1(2)(b) the sheriff of the district or county in which the seizure was made`

DECLARE `s 488.1(3) applicant` IS ONE OF
    `s 488.1(3) the Attorney General`
    `s 488.1(3) the client`
    `s 488.1(3) the lawyer on behalf of the client`
    `s 488.1(3) someone else`

-- covers: 488.1(3), 488.1(3)(a)
-- fork: F7,G1
-- jural: the client, the lawyer on behalf of the client, or the Attorney General > a judge > power
-- src:9926 | (3) Where a document has been seized and placed in custody under subsection (2), the Attorney General or the client or the lawyer on behalf of the client, may
-- src:9927 | (a) within fourteen days from the day the document was so placed in custody, apply, on two days notice of motion to all other persons entitled to make application, to a judge for an order
-- src:9928 | (i) appointing a place and a day, not later than twenty-one days after the date of the order, for the determination of the question whether the document should be disclosed, and
-- src:9929 | (ii) requiring the custodian to produce the document to the judge at that time and place;
-- src:9930 | (b) serve a copy of the order on all other persons entitled to make application and on the custodian within six days of the date on which it was made; and
-- src:9931 | (c) if he has proceeded as authorized by paragraph (b), apply, at the appointed time and place, for an order determining the question.
@ref s 488.1(3) (src:9926-9931)
-- (a) apply within fourteen days from the day the document was placed in custody, on two days notice of motion to all other persons entitled; the fourteen days and the two days are periods the text
-- fixes in its own words, so outside them the answer is JUST FALSE (ruling of 2026-11-05 (a); fork F7 names the other reading for a grant, NOTHING).
GIVEN applicant IS A `s 488.1(3) applicant`
      `the document has been seized and placed in custody under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the document was placed in custody` IS A DATE
      `the day of the application` IS A DATE
      `the days of notice of motion given to all other persons entitled to make application` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 488.1(3)(a) the person may apply to a judge for an order appointing a place and a day for the determination of the question and requiring the custodian to produce the document` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF applicant EQUALS `s 488.1(3) someone else` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF NOT `the document has been seized and placed in custody under subsection (2)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF `the day of the application` GREATER THAN `s 488.1(3)(a) the last day to apply to a judge` `the day the document was placed in custody` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within fourteen days from the day the document was so placed in custody, apply"
        IF `the days of notice of motion given to all other persons entitled to make application` LESS THAN 2 THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on two days notice of motion to all other persons entitled to make application"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 488.1(3)(a) (the fourteen days) (src:9926-9927)
GIVEN `the day the document was placed in custody` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 488.1(3)(a) the last day to apply to a judge` MEANS
    `the day the document was placed in custody` PLUS 14

@ref s 488.1(3)(a)(i) (the twenty-one days) (src:9926-9929)
GIVEN `the date of the order` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 488.1(3)(a)(i) the latest day that may be appointed for the determination of the question` MEANS
    `the date of the order` PLUS 21

-- covers: 488.1(3)(b)
-- jural: all other persons entitled to make application, and the custodian > the client, the lawyer or the Attorney General who applied > right
@ref s 488.1(3)(b) (the six days) (src:9930)
GIVEN `the date on which the order was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 488.1(3)(b) the last day to serve a copy of the order on all other persons entitled to make application and on the custodian` MEANS
    `the date on which the order was made` PLUS 6

GIVEN `the date on which the order was made` IS A DATE
      `the day the copy of the order is served` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 488.1(3)(b) the copy of the order is served within six days` MEANS
    `the day the copy of the order is served` AT MOST `s 488.1(3)(b) the last day to serve a copy of the order on all other persons entitled to make application and on the custodian` `the date on which the order was made`

-- covers: 488.1(3)(c)
-- fork: F1
-- jural: the client, the lawyer on behalf of the client, or the Attorney General > a judge > power
@ref s 488.1(3)(c) (the second application) (src:9931)
GIVEN applicant IS A `s 488.1(3) applicant`
      `the person has served a copy of the order as authorized by paragraph (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 488.1(3)(c) the person may apply at the appointed time and place for an order determining the question` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF applicant EQUALS `s 488.1(3) someone else` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF `the person has served a copy of the order as authorized by paragraph (b)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

§ `Section 488.1 -- The judge's disposition`

-- covers: 488.1(4), 488.1(4)(a)
-- fork: F1
-- jural: the Attorney General and the person who objects > a judge > right
-- src:9934 | (a) may, if the judge considers it necessary to determine the question whether the document should be disclosed, inspect the document;
-- src:9935 | (b) where the judge is of the opinion that it would materially assist him in deciding whether or not the document is privileged, may allow the Attorney General to inspect the document;
@ref s 488.1(4)(a) and (b) (src:9934-9935)
GIVEN `the judge considers it necessary to determine the question whether the document should be disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 488.1(4)(a) the judge may inspect the document` MEANS
    IF `the judge considers it necessary to determine the question whether the document should be disclosed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- covers: 488.1(4)(b)
-- fork: F1
-- jural: a judge > the person who objects to the disclosure > power
@ref s 488.1(4)(b) (src:9935)
GIVEN `the judge is of the opinion that it would materially assist in deciding whether or not the document is privileged` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 488.1(4)(b) the judge may allow the Attorney General to inspect the document` MEANS
    IF `the judge is of the opinion that it would materially assist in deciding whether or not the document is privileged`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- covers: 488.1(4)(c)
-- jural: the Attorney General and the person who objects to the disclosure > a judge > right
-- src:9936 | (c) shall allow the Attorney General and the person who objects to the disclosure of the document to make representations; and
@ref s 488.1(4)(c) (src:9936)
GIVEN `the application is made under paragraph (3)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 488.1(4)(c) the judge shall allow the Attorney General and the person who objects to the disclosure of the document to make representations` MEANS
    IF `the application is made under paragraph (3)(c)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On an application under paragraph (3)(c), the judge"

DECLARE `s 488.1(4)(d) order` IS ONE OF
    `s 488.1(4)(d)(i) repackage and reseal the document and order the custodian to deliver it to the lawyer who claimed the solicitor-client privilege or to the client`
    `s 488.1(4)(d)(ii) order the custodian to deliver the document to the officer who seized it or some other person designated by the Attorney General, subject to such restrictions or conditions as the judge deems appropriate`

-- covers: 488.1(4)(d), 488.1(4) closing words
-- jural: the client > a judge > right
-- src:9937 | (d) shall determine the question summarily and,
-- src:9938 | (i) if the judge is of the opinion that the document should not be disclosed, ensure that it is repackaged and resealed and order the custodian to deliver the document to the lawyer who claimed the solicitor-client privilege or to the client, or
-- src:9939 | (ii) if the judge is of the opinion that the document should be disclosed, order the custodian to deliver the document to the officer who seized the document or some other person designated by the Attorney General, subject to such restrictions or conditions as the judge deems appropriate,
-- src:9940 | and shall, at the same time, deliver concise reasons for the determination in which the nature of the document is described without divulging the details thereof.
@ref s 488.1(4)(d) (src:9937-9940)
GIVEN `the application is made under paragraph (3)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is of the opinion that the document should not be disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is of the opinion that the document should be disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 488.1(4)(d) order`
`s 488.1(4)(d) the order the judge shall make` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the application is made under paragraph (3)(c)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF `the judge is of the opinion that the document should not be disclosed` AND NOT `the judge is of the opinion that the document should be disclosed` THEN JUST `s 488.1(4)(d)(i) repackage and reseal the document and order the custodian to deliver it to the lawyer who claimed the solicitor-client privilege or to the client`
        IF `the judge is of the opinion that the document should be disclosed` AND NOT `the judge is of the opinion that the document should not be disclosed` THEN JUST `s 488.1(4)(d)(ii) order the custodian to deliver the document to the officer who seized it or some other person designated by the Attorney General, subject to such restrictions or conditions as the judge deems appropriate`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent)

@ref s 488.1(4) closing words (reasons) (src:9940)
GIVEN `the application is made under paragraph (3)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 488.1(4) the judge shall, at the same time, deliver concise reasons for the determination in which the nature of the document is described without divulging the details` MEANS
    IF `the application is made under paragraph (3)(c)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On an application under paragraph (3)(c), the judge"

-- covers: 488.1(5)
-- jural: the client > any person who would use the document in evidence > immunity
