@ref s 488.1(5) (src:9942)
GIVEN `the judge determines pursuant to paragraph (4)(d) that a solicitor-client privilege exists in respect of the document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the client consents to its admission in evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the privilege is otherwise lost` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 488.1(5) the document remains privileged and inadmissible as evidence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the judge determines pursuant to paragraph (4)(d) that a solicitor-client privilege exists in respect of the document` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF `the client consents to its admission in evidence` OR `the privilege is otherwise lost` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the client consents to its admission in evidence or the privilege is otherwise lost"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- covers: 488.1(6)
-- jural: the Attorney General > a judge > right
