@ref s 488.1(6) (src:9944)
GIVEN `the judge is applied to by the Attorney General` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that no application has been made under paragraph (3)(a) or that following such an application no further application has been made under paragraph (3)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 488.1(6) the judge shall order the custodian to deliver the document to the officer who seized it or to some other person designated by the Attorney General` MEANS
    IF `the judge is applied to by the Attorney General` AND `the judge is satisfied that no application has been made under paragraph (3)(a) or that following such an application no further application has been made under paragraph (3)(c)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a document has been seized and placed in custody under subsection (2) and a judge, on the application of the Attorney General, is satisfied"

-- covers: 488.1(7)
-- fork: G1
-- jural: a person with an application under paragraph (3)(c) > a judge > power
